- slice() se page-wise images nikalo
- totalPages calculate karo
- Page change pe setCurrentPage() call karo
- Prev, Next, 1 2 3 buttons render karo using Array.from()

1.  useState se page track karna
    const [currentPage, setCurrentPage] = useState(1);  // starting from page 1
    const itemsPerPage = 12; // ek page pe 12 image

2.  Array ka slice() use karke 12 images nikaal lo
    const paginatedImages = galleryImages.slice(
          (currentPage - 1) * itemsPerPage,
          currentPage * itemsPerPage
        );
      eg - Agar currentPage = 1 => slice(0, 12); // 0 to 11th index → 12 images
           Agar currentPage = 2 => slice(12, 24); // 12 to 23rd index

3.  Kitne total pages banenge ? 
          const totalPages = Math.ceil(galleryImages.length / itemsPerPage);
         // agar 25 images hain toh 3 pages banenge (12 + 12 + 1)

4. Page change hone pe setCurrentPage 
         const handlePageChange = (page) => {
            if (page >= 1 && page <= totalPages) {
              setCurrentPage(page); // page update
              window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' }); // page scroll to top
            }
          };

5.  Pagination Button ka JSX - 
          <div className="flex justify-center gap-3 mt-10 flex-wrap">

              {/* Prev Button */}
              <button
                onClick={() => handlePageChange(currentPage - 1)}
                disabled={currentPage === 1} >
                Prev
              </button>
            
              {/* Page Number Buttons */}
              {Array.from({ length: totalPages }, (_, i) => (                           // Array bnao of length {totalpages} -> hr idx p traverse kro -> on click button -> ek callback func call kro
                <button                                                                        // _ ka mtlb hai — pehla argument (value) kaam ka nahi, to ignore kiya.
                  key={i}
                  onClick={() => handlePageChange(i + 1)}                                      // i + 1 isliye, kyunki index 0 se start hota hai, but pages 1 se.
                  className={currentPage === i + 1 ? 'bg-green-700 text-white' : ''} > 
                  {i + 1}
                </button>
              ))}
            
              {/* Next Button */}
              <button
                onClick={() => handlePageChange(currentPage + 1)}
                disabled={currentPage === totalPages} >
                Next
              </button>
        
        </div>
        
        
// How to map images to imageCard component --> simple - 

        <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
                {paginatedImages.map((item, index) => (
                  <ImageCard key={index} image={item.image} />
                ))}
        </div>       
